// mecatl driver API: the remote agent-definition source protocol.
//
// AgentSourceService is the wire seam behind the harness's
// `tool.AgentDefSource` (engine/tool/agentsource.go): an operator-run driver
// process serves named subagent specialists (a prompt persona + a scoped tool
// allowlist + a model + a permission mode + run limits) in place of the local
// <name>.md discovery. No path, directory, or root concept crosses this wire;
// where the driver keeps its definitions is its private business. The driver
// sits at the SAME trust tier as an operator-configured agents directory — a
// def body steers the model like AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md, so point the harness
// only at a driver you trust.
//
// Driver contract (pinned by the engine/adapter/sourceconformance suite,
// which remote drivers run over their client):
//   - ListAgentDefs returns the definitions sorted by name, unique, and
//     STABLE for the life of the source (SNAPSHOT semantics — the harness
//     resolves once at build and bakes per-def child engines; there is no
//     watch/reload seam).
//   - A ListAgentDefs fault at harness BUILD time is FATAL (loud-misconfig
//     posture: an explicitly configured driver that cannot answer is a
//     misconfiguration). There is no runtime re-fetch.
